{
  "configuration_id": "config_026",
  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_047 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) at 0.706 accuracy, dramatically outperforming all scgpt-based configs (~0.52–0.54). The only untested design axis holding all other parameters at their best-known values is aggregation: transformer vs. avgpool. With scgpt, avgpool beat transformer by ~2 pts (0.542 vs 0.520), but scvi_n200 produces a fundamentally different variational 200-dim representation where attention-based aggregation could capture inter-profile interactions that simple averaging misses. This single-variable change from the best config is the most interpretable and highest-value test: if transformer helps, we push accuracy above 0.706; if not, we confirm avgpool is optimal and can spend remaining budget on other axes (e.g., concat fusion or singleprofile). Expected cost: ~4–5 GPU hours (comparable to config_047's 4.82, with a modest increase from transformer attention layers), keeping total well within a reasonable budget for the remaining 3 experiments."
}

